WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.675
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.675 --> 00:03.344
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION AND
SHAMEFUL ACTS ARE NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:03.344 --> 00:04.970
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:10.267 --> 00:13.896
Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth

00:13.896 --> 00:16.899
Right now is always
the best of the season

00:17.107 --> 00:20.569
Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning

00:20.653 --> 00:24.114
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

00:24.114 --> 00:27.409
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

00:27.451 --> 00:29.537
Ever Endless

00:30.746 --> 00:32.414
Ever Endless

00:34.166 --> 00:35.709
Ever Endless

00:37.586 --> 00:38.963
Ever Endless

00:39.630 --> 00:44.426
Mon-Tues-Weds-Thurs-Fri,
my life knows no variety

00:44.426 --> 00:45.845
Ever Endless

00:46.262 --> 00:51.058
Sat-Sun, wake up in the afternoon
with only my smartphone to surf

00:51.058 --> 00:52.643
Ever Endless

00:52.643 --> 00:54.061
All my limbs' been giving in

00:54.061 --> 00:55.896
Kalbi's a burden
like my lumber spine

00:55.896 --> 00:57.481
Doing family
service with irises dim

00:57.481 --> 00:59.108
But you know that
I'll go all the way

00:59.525 --> 01:02.695
Glitter, shimmer,
the light's shining

01:02.987 --> 01:06.532
Let's give it one more chance

01:06.532 --> 01:09.994
Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth

01:10.202 --> 01:12.997
Right now is always
the best of the season

01:13.205 --> 01:16.834
Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning

01:16.834 --> 01:19.837
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

01:20.087 --> 01:22.214
Youth is when you never...

01:22.214 --> 01:23.716
stop chasing your own values

01:23.716 --> 01:25.384
Our youth's eternal

01:25.384 --> 01:26.969
the color never fades with age

01:26.969 --> 01:28.846
Youth is when you keep...

01:28.846 --> 01:30.389
getting lost along the way

01:30.389 --> 01:33.934
Youth is Forever

01:38.105 --> 01:38.731
Alright!

01:39.356 --> 01:41.442
The Next-Term
Professor Candidate!

01:41.442 --> 01:44.028
This is a lecture by
me, Ushironomiya!

01:44.028 --> 01:47.198
Remember to savor every
minute and every second!

01:47.615 --> 01:51.035
Today, we'll be running
the Charpy Impact Test.

01:51.243 --> 01:52.620
Yeees.

01:52.620 --> 01:55.164
This is a method to
calculate the needed energy

01:55.289 --> 01:59.376
to destroy the sample, based on
the difference in potential energy.

01:59.627 --> 02:02.504
But it's just a
simple experiment.

02:02.504 --> 02:04.590
The equations are basic too.

02:04.590 --> 02:06.759
Looks like this
report's gonna be easy.

02:06.759 --> 02:07.676
No doubt about it.

02:07.843 --> 02:10.137
You all look awfully relaxed.

02:10.137 --> 02:11.889
Well, of course.

02:11.889 --> 02:13.974
This is only high
school-level physics.

02:13.974 --> 02:16.435
It's nowhere near our level.

02:16.435 --> 02:18.979
It's almost harder to
screw up than succeed.

02:18.979 --> 02:19.980
I see.

02:20.189 --> 02:23.067
So you're saying you'd never
mess up a lab of this level?

02:23.067 --> 02:24.568
- Of course.
- Of course.

02:24.568 --> 02:26.028
I see, I see.

02:26.237 --> 02:27.947
Then, use this.

02:28.489 --> 02:29.990
Huh? A cushion?

02:29.990 --> 02:31.617
What's this for?

02:31.617 --> 02:34.119
Do you want us to do
the lab while seated?

02:34.286 --> 02:35.704
That's not quite it.

02:38.165 --> 02:39.667
If you're so excellent,

02:39.667 --> 02:43.087
can you calculate a height where
your nether regions won't get crushed?

02:43.087 --> 02:45.548
How can this guy say
such terrifying things?

02:45.548 --> 02:47.675
This is just a penalty
game at this point.

02:47.675 --> 02:49.426
Are you even
human, you bastard?!

02:50.761 --> 02:52.596
It's fine, isn't it?

02:52.763 --> 02:55.558
As if any of you will ever get
a chance to use them anyway.

02:55.558 --> 02:57.560
- Are you looking for a fight!?
- Are you looking for a fight!?

02:57.560 --> 02:59.395
You have four trials in this.

02:59.395 --> 03:03.607
Fail to destroy the sample even
once, and I won't give you any credit!

03:05.109 --> 03:06.443
That bastard.

03:06.443 --> 03:08.279
And we have to do it four times.

03:08.279 --> 03:10.990
Just hope Yamamoto's
crotch can last until the end.

03:11.448 --> 03:12.867
We're doing it together, right?

03:12.867 --> 03:14.743
We each get one turn, right?

03:14.910 --> 03:16.245
So what should we do?

03:16.245 --> 03:18.539
We're not even
allowed to mess up once.

03:18.539 --> 03:20.708
We can't test it
at a low heights.

03:21.125 --> 03:22.209
Which means...

03:22.418 --> 03:25.254
- The first trial is guaranteed death!
- The first trial is guaranteed death!

03:25.254 --> 03:27.298
Start with Yamamoto
as he's prepared.

03:27.298 --> 03:28.591
Wait, wait, wait!

03:28.591 --> 03:31.343
Start with Imamura
since he's uninterest in 3D.

03:31.594 --> 03:32.469
You've got a point.

03:32.469 --> 03:33.387
What did you say?

03:33.846 --> 03:34.471
Hmph.

03:34.471 --> 03:36.974
Listen up, my crotch
is very important

03:36.974 --> 03:40.311
to the middle school girls that
cherish me as their onii-chan.

03:40.311 --> 03:41.896
Alright, let's go with this guy.

03:41.896 --> 03:44.398
We ought to destroy it
before he becomes a criminal.

03:44.398 --> 03:45.858
Stop it, you guys!

03:45.858 --> 03:47.234
Who's stopping?

03:47.234 --> 03:48.569
You prospective criminal!

03:48.569 --> 03:50.571
Give it up and prepare
to get smashed.

03:52.865 --> 03:55.117
You guys should
go with Kitahara first!

03:56.702 --> 03:58.287
He'll do something with Kote...

04:00.497 --> 04:02.917
Alright, it seems
Kouhei has agreed.

04:02.917 --> 04:04.376
Let's proceed with
the experiment.

04:04.376 --> 04:05.544
Ah, yeah.

04:05.544 --> 04:07.796
That bastard is the devil...

04:11.550 --> 04:12.885
You guys?!

04:13.260 --> 04:14.803
So he woke up.

04:14.803 --> 04:16.805
Hurry up with the preparations!

04:16.805 --> 04:18.557
Listen to me...

04:18.557 --> 04:20.017
Actually... I'm...

04:21.685 --> 04:23.270
The equipment is good to go!

04:23.270 --> 04:25.064
All measurements complete!

04:26.565 --> 04:28.400
Alright! Commence experiment!

04:28.400 --> 04:30.945
Stop it! You bastard!

04:33.948 --> 04:36.408
In honor of our
fallen hero, salute!

04:45.668 --> 04:47.836
So 150° is too high, eh?

04:47.836 --> 04:50.256
Next time, we can
probably set it a bit lower.

04:50.256 --> 04:52.550
I'm just glad we
got some good data.

04:52.883 --> 04:54.927
So, next up is...

04:55.094 --> 04:58.347
Let me choose...
the next one to go.

05:00.599 --> 05:01.475
Huh?

05:01.767 --> 05:02.726
It's all yours.

05:02.726 --> 05:05.688
In your dreams, let's play
rock-paper-scissors to decide!

05:05.688 --> 05:07.398
What are you
saying, you shithead?

05:07.398 --> 05:10.109
This is the will of our great
fallen hero, you piece of shit.

05:10.109 --> 05:11.944
You guys are the real bastards!

05:11.986 --> 05:14.446
Kouhei, we're
best friends, right?

05:15.447 --> 05:17.658
Kitahara... don't
tell anyone this...

05:17.658 --> 05:21.328
But I have a past
report for this lab.

05:22.204 --> 05:24.164
MECHANIC OF MATERIALS
All the equations are written down.

05:24.164 --> 05:25.457
CHARPY IMPACT TEST Oh...

05:25.624 --> 05:27.877
Just follow the report.

05:27.877 --> 05:29.378
It'll be fine.

05:31.547 --> 05:33.215
According to this report,

05:33.215 --> 05:36.135
the angle should be 138°.

05:36.385 --> 05:37.678
That's quite high.

05:37.887 --> 05:39.096
Now, let's do it.

05:39.096 --> 05:39.638
Yeah.

05:39.638 --> 05:41.015
By the way, Kitahara.

05:41.015 --> 05:41.724
Huh?

05:42.016 --> 05:44.977
BIG MISTAKES!! RE-SUBMIT IT!!
This is the evaluation of that report.

05:45.477 --> 05:46.645
Huh?

05:50.149 --> 05:53.319
Did I ever say that
it was a good report?

05:53.319 --> 05:54.820
I suppose you didn't.

05:54.820 --> 05:56.906
You technically didn't lie.

05:56.906 --> 05:59.074
So, the next person will be...

05:59.074 --> 06:00.117
You first, right?

06:00.117 --> 06:01.368
No, no, after you.

06:01.368 --> 06:03.245
You guys...

06:03.454 --> 06:05.039
What do you want,
you failed corpse?

06:05.039 --> 06:06.624
You have a will or something?

06:06.624 --> 06:08.709
Let me see that report.

06:08.709 --> 06:10.294
I don't mind.

06:12.004 --> 06:13.130
As I thought.

06:13.297 --> 06:14.048
What is it?

06:14.048 --> 06:15.966
Ah, this report...

06:16.133 --> 06:18.177
Looks like the
equation was correct.

06:18.844 --> 06:21.055
They made a small
calculation error here.

06:21.055 --> 06:22.139
Let me see.

06:22.348 --> 06:23.516
You're right.

06:23.516 --> 06:26.936
- Then if we recalculate it...
- wouldn't there be a risk?

06:27.269 --> 06:29.897
Wait a minute,
let me recalculate.

06:30.231 --> 06:31.857
By the way, Nojima is next.

06:31.857 --> 06:33.609
W-Why me?

06:34.026 --> 06:36.529
This is an order
from a fallen hero.

06:36.529 --> 06:38.280
Be grateful and accept your job.

06:38.447 --> 06:41.575
Besides, it's better to
have longer legs in this.

06:42.284 --> 06:42.993
Huh?

06:43.619 --> 06:44.787
Could it be...

06:44.787 --> 06:47.164
that Yamamoto
actually has longer...

06:47.164 --> 06:48.707
Alright, I'm up!

06:49.250 --> 06:51.418
Got it, it's 134°.

06:51.418 --> 06:53.504
Okay, let's adjust the height.

06:53.504 --> 06:55.756
Although I can't say
I trust your math...

06:55.756 --> 06:58.551
Don't worry, I got
the same answer.

06:58.759 --> 07:00.928
Even if we're the ones
who did the match,

07:00.928 --> 07:03.639
it's reassuring that our
answers match, right?

07:03.639 --> 07:05.307
Yeah, you're right.

07:05.558 --> 07:07.560
It's at 134° now.

07:07.893 --> 07:08.561
Oh.

07:08.561 --> 07:10.354
Don't worry so much.

07:10.354 --> 07:12.857
Our calculations
were perfect, so relax.

07:16.360 --> 07:18.571
These pricks are lying
through their teeth!

07:20.155 --> 07:21.991
Now, you're the only one left.

07:21.991 --> 07:24.326
Let's try around 133°.

07:24.326 --> 07:25.411
No, no, no!

07:25.411 --> 07:27.621
You already know
the answer is 101°!

07:27.621 --> 07:29.331
Why are you raising it?

07:29.874 --> 07:31.166
About that answer,

07:31.166 --> 07:33.836
it needs to be multiplied
by the coefficient of N.

07:33.836 --> 07:35.254
The coefficient of N?

07:35.588 --> 07:37.047
That's right.

07:38.465 --> 07:42.136
It stands for "the
coefficient of Nastiness."

07:45.598 --> 07:46.599
Professor!

07:46.849 --> 07:48.934
We were wrong, professor!

07:48.934 --> 07:51.228
We're sorry that we
underestimated the lab!

07:51.228 --> 07:54.648
Please teach us about the
mechanics of materials, professor!

07:56.317 --> 07:59.111
Have you finally realized
your own inexperience?

07:59.111 --> 07:59.945
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

07:59.945 --> 08:01.030
So professor!

08:01.030 --> 08:03.449
Please lead us
inexperienced students!

08:03.449 --> 08:04.617
We beg of you!

08:05.868 --> 08:08.037
I see, so be it!

08:08.037 --> 08:11.040
I'll give you the special
privilege of being taught by me!

08:13.459 --> 08:14.960
Then please lead by example.

08:14.960 --> 08:16.754
Ah, spread your legs a bit.

08:16.754 --> 08:19.381
If you don't put some
strength in your abs, you'll die.

08:20.424 --> 08:22.426
You really are all fools.

08:22.676 --> 08:25.888
How could I
possibly miscalculate!

08:25.888 --> 08:28.891
Set α to 101°!

08:28.891 --> 08:29.475
Yes!

08:29.475 --> 08:31.185
As you wish, professor.

08:31.477 --> 08:33.187
Here we go, professor.

08:33.187 --> 08:35.064
Sure, start it
whenever you want.

08:35.356 --> 08:37.441
It will stop 1 mm in
front of my crotch.

08:37.441 --> 08:40.778
Cast your eyes upon the
accuracy of my calculations.

08:46.867 --> 08:48.327
WEIGHT

08:52.248 --> 08:53.499
Which means...

08:53.958 --> 08:59.797
the additional energy of the added mass
will be added directly to the total energy.

09:01.006 --> 09:03.425
If that's... 300 g...

09:04.510 --> 09:07.179
at a height of 73
cm to be equal...

09:07.888 --> 09:09.014
I see.

09:09.014 --> 09:10.558
I truly learned this first-hand.

09:10.558 --> 09:12.351
A truly authentic experiment.

09:12.351 --> 09:15.104
I won't forget this equation
for the rest of my life.

09:15.479 --> 09:17.940
This school is full of morons.

09:17.940 --> 09:19.441
THE CHARPY IMPACT TEST
HAS A HIGH RATE OF ERROR.

09:19.441 --> 09:20.985
ONLY TRY THIS AT HOME
AFTER SPECIAL TRAINING.

09:22.528 --> 09:24.196
The moon is beautiful, isn't it?

09:24.947 --> 09:25.948
So much I could die

09:26.156 --> 09:28.951
Now then, does anyone know
where this song comes from?

09:30.244 --> 09:31.787
It's from a booze commercial.

09:31.787 --> 09:32.705
Wrong.

09:32.705 --> 09:33.998
Then what could it be?

09:33.998 --> 09:36.041
Just which anime song is it?

09:36.041 --> 09:37.418
It's not an anime song.

09:37.960 --> 09:38.794
A hint!

09:38.794 --> 09:40.004
Give us a hint.

09:40.004 --> 09:41.797
I guess I have to.

09:41.797 --> 09:43.924
There's a TV show that I like...

09:43.924 --> 09:46.177
The theme song from
a reality dating show?

09:46.177 --> 09:47.386
How'd you know?

09:47.511 --> 09:49.889
Then my song is next.

09:49.889 --> 09:50.681
Anime song.

09:50.681 --> 09:52.266
At least wait 'til
you've heard it.

09:52.266 --> 09:53.934
Let's have Chisa go next.

09:54.476 --> 09:55.186
Huh?

09:56.353 --> 09:57.479
I...

09:57.646 --> 09:59.940
What do you usually
listen to, Chisa?

09:59.940 --> 10:01.400
I'm kinda curious.

10:01.400 --> 10:04.653
I just listen to normal
J-pop, nothing interesting.

10:04.653 --> 10:07.198
We'll be the judge if
it's interesting or not.

10:07.198 --> 10:07.990
That's right.

10:15.581 --> 10:17.124
The sound of the ocean?

10:17.124 --> 10:18.417
Are you serious?

10:18.417 --> 10:20.544
How is this normal J-pop?

10:20.961 --> 10:24.381
There's also "a flowing
river," "underwater sounds..."

10:24.381 --> 10:26.217
So anything's fine
as long as it's water?

10:26.217 --> 10:28.928
None of this even music, is it?

10:29.470 --> 10:31.931
As expected, Chisa does
have a screw or two loose.

10:32.640 --> 10:35.267
Do you really want
a song with lyrics?

10:35.267 --> 10:36.977
If you even have one.

10:36.977 --> 10:38.521
Fine, here you go.

10:41.315 --> 10:42.066
Oh.

10:42.066 --> 10:43.567
Sounds like a normal song.

10:43.567 --> 10:46.111
But the tune is really cheesy.

10:46.111 --> 10:48.280
I've never heard
this song before.

10:48.280 --> 10:50.366
What song is this, Kotegawa?

10:51.575 --> 10:53.077
Stop the music, Chisa.

10:53.869 --> 10:56.038
Otherwise, I'll grope
the heck outta you.

10:56.914 --> 10:58.040
Huh? What?

10:58.040 --> 10:59.833
Kitahara, you know this song?

11:00.000 --> 11:01.669
This song is...

11:01.669 --> 11:06.841
In 10 or 20 years from now...

11:06.841 --> 11:09.718
Iori's middle
school composition.

11:11.595 --> 11:12.930
Kouhei, restrain him.

11:12.930 --> 11:14.306
Already on it.

11:14.306 --> 11:17.059
Let me go! Or
just kill me already!

11:17.059 --> 11:18.561
But how did you get this?

11:18.811 --> 11:21.689
I wrote a letter to
Shiori-chan a while back.

11:22.106 --> 11:25.776
When I told her that Iori wasn't
planning on going home this summer,

11:25.776 --> 11:27.111
she sent me this.

11:27.361 --> 11:28.737
I see.

11:28.737 --> 11:31.115
Shiori!

11:31.115 --> 11:32.241
In search of tomorrow

11:32.241 --> 11:35.035
One day for my sake

11:40.708 --> 11:42.626
Looks like the rich
peeps already arrived.

11:42.626 --> 11:43.878
They're really early.

11:44.086 --> 11:48.799
But I can't believe PaB's using an
abandoned school for summer camp.

11:48.799 --> 11:51.844
I found a pretty good spot.

11:52.094 --> 11:55.806
But what were you searching for
that led to an elementary school?

11:56.807 --> 11:57.641
Huh?

11:58.184 --> 12:01.478
But a bonfire in the
schoolyard sounds amazing.

12:01.854 --> 12:04.648
It'll be my first time
sleeping in a classroom bed.

12:04.648 --> 12:06.775
And we can go nuts
with the fireworks.

12:07.067 --> 12:10.487
This time for sure, my
album of memories...

12:14.491 --> 12:15.826
Test of courage.

12:15.826 --> 12:17.745
Make your way to the rooftop.

12:18.120 --> 12:20.664
My... album...

12:20.664 --> 12:22.750
Just give up on that album.

12:22.750 --> 12:25.294
I'm staying here
until it's over.

12:25.419 --> 12:27.171
What's there to be afraid of?

12:27.171 --> 12:30.007
They probably messed
around while setting it up.

12:30.925 --> 12:34.803
And also, we've all sworn off
alcohol until the event is over.

12:35.179 --> 12:36.597
This is bad.

12:38.057 --> 12:40.017
GIRLS' COURSE

12:40.309 --> 12:41.894
So you guys are going that way.

12:44.897 --> 12:45.856
Then...

12:46.148 --> 12:48.067
we'll go this way.

12:48.067 --> 12:50.027
IDIOTS' COURSE

12:50.319 --> 12:52.738
Wait, seems like we
don't go this way either.

12:52.738 --> 12:55.407
No no, it's clearly
meant just for you.

12:55.407 --> 12:57.826
That's enough, you two
hurry up and get going.

13:06.001 --> 13:08.379
T-They sure got the
atmosphere down.

13:08.379 --> 13:09.797
It feels pretty authentic.

13:13.425 --> 13:14.969
Looks like a French doll.

13:14.969 --> 13:17.096
T-That scared me.

13:20.307 --> 13:23.394
I thought you'd be bad
with this kinda thing.

13:23.394 --> 13:26.856
To me, meeting
someone new is scarier.

13:27.064 --> 13:29.859
Yeah, you're that
kind of person.

13:30.484 --> 13:31.277
Huh?

13:31.277 --> 13:34.196
Ahhh! Stop it!

13:35.531 --> 13:36.866
That was...

13:36.866 --> 13:38.200
Imamura-kun's voice?

13:38.617 --> 13:41.245
He must've seen
something really scary.

13:42.997 --> 13:46.375
It'll damage her neck if
you hang her like that!

13:46.375 --> 13:48.210
Shut up. Let's hurry
up and get going.

13:53.340 --> 13:54.925
A Japanese doll?

13:54.925 --> 13:56.177
Be careful, Aina.

13:56.177 --> 13:56.719
Huh?

13:56.969 --> 13:59.597
Usually when we're
focused on what's ahead...

13:59.597 --> 14:01.265
something will come from...

14:02.308 --> 14:06.228
Something cold and slimy!

14:06.520 --> 14:08.147
It's just konnyaku.

14:10.065 --> 14:12.026
Figures are delicate.

14:12.151 --> 14:13.819
If you treat them like that...

14:13.819 --> 14:15.154
Yeah, yeah.

14:16.030 --> 14:17.448
A Japanese doll, eh?

14:17.615 --> 14:19.158
Be careful, Kitahara.

14:19.241 --> 14:20.701
Yeah, I know.

14:20.701 --> 14:22.119
Something's going to come...

14:22.536 --> 14:23.746
As expected.

14:23.954 --> 14:25.748
Is this all they've got?

14:27.750 --> 14:30.294
USED

14:32.171 --> 14:35.007
Looks like those two
are bad with horror.

14:35.007 --> 14:36.926
Is.. that true?

14:41.055 --> 14:41.805
Heh?

14:42.431 --> 14:43.390
What's wrong?

14:43.766 --> 14:46.936
Just now, some
kinda white shadow...

14:46.936 --> 14:47.686
Huh?

14:55.986 --> 14:58.948
I-Is that you, Azusa-san?

15:05.037 --> 15:05.996
AAAAA-

15:05.996 --> 15:08.457
- AAAHHH!
- A-Aina!

15:12.586 --> 15:13.337
Oh.

15:13.337 --> 15:14.755
Just now, was that...

15:14.755 --> 15:16.215
a female ghost?

15:16.465 --> 15:19.176
If it's a real ghost,
there's no problem.

15:19.677 --> 15:23.430
But if it isn't...

15:31.981 --> 15:33.482
- I'll leave this one to you.
- Like I'd let you!

15:36.944 --> 15:38.487
Don't come any closer!

15:38.821 --> 15:41.448
Even if you are
a female ghost...

15:43.951 --> 15:45.327
Ugh...

15:45.327 --> 15:49.748
No!

15:50.457 --> 15:52.459
Cheers!

15:54.461 --> 15:56.005
So? Was it scary?

15:56.297 --> 15:57.882
I was terrified.

15:58.007 --> 16:00.718
That was a traumatic experience.

16:00.718 --> 16:03.429
That should be
straight up illegal.

16:04.847 --> 16:07.016
I'm just glad you enjoyed it.

16:11.687 --> 16:13.147
Io... Iorin...

16:13.147 --> 16:14.356
Who you calling Iorin?

16:14.732 --> 16:16.817
There's this
bluish-white flame...

16:16.817 --> 16:18.027
- Oh.
- You're right.

16:18.152 --> 16:20.446
Why are you guys so calm?

16:20.446 --> 16:21.488
Well, calm down.

16:23.407 --> 16:24.491
- As you can see.
- As you can see.

16:25.117 --> 16:25.951
Ah...

16:26.327 --> 16:28.787
Whoops, so this is Spirytus.

16:28.787 --> 16:30.748
So this is non-flammable water.

16:31.248 --> 16:33.250
Hey, Iori, Kouhei.

16:33.500 --> 16:36.295
Help us set up the bonfire!

16:36.545 --> 16:37.796
Roger.

16:40.508 --> 16:42.301
A bonfire.

16:42.301 --> 16:43.677
So nostalgic.

16:43.677 --> 16:46.305
It's almost like camping
in elementary school.

16:47.681 --> 16:49.517
Ah, it's lit.

16:55.481 --> 16:57.024
What a nice atmosphere.

16:57.024 --> 16:59.276
Like a scene straight
out of a teen drama.

16:59.527 --> 17:02.530
Now if only a boy would
come offer me his hand...

17:02.530 --> 17:03.697
"Let's dance."

17:03.697 --> 17:05.366
and then we could
do a folk dance...

17:05.699 --> 17:06.367
Hey.

17:06.367 --> 17:07.826
Huh? What is it?

17:07.826 --> 17:10.287
Since we're here, let's dance.

17:24.969 --> 17:26.428
Limbo!

17:26.428 --> 17:27.596
I knew it.

17:27.847 --> 17:30.850
I should've known better than
to get my hopes up in this club.

17:30.850 --> 17:31.767
Hopes?

17:31.767 --> 17:33.727
What are you talking about?

17:52.746 --> 17:54.582
They're sure good at it.

17:54.957 --> 17:56.000
Yeah, well...

17:56.542 --> 17:57.376
Want a drink?

17:57.626 --> 17:58.878
Yeah, I'll have one.

18:21.192 --> 18:24.486
My foot caught on
something and I slipped...

18:25.029 --> 18:26.780
Was there something
on the ground?

18:27.156 --> 18:29.617
USED

18:29.742 --> 18:31.827
Something... like this...

18:31.827 --> 18:33.078
Are you okay, Chisa?

18:33.370 --> 18:36.207
Don't worry, it was
just an accident.

18:41.337 --> 18:43.505
Do you really
have to go that far?

18:45.257 --> 18:47.718
Hey, Chisa. Even if
you're just gargling...

18:47.718 --> 18:49.512
pouring that in your
mouth so many times...

18:50.179 --> 18:51.555
I'm completely fine.

18:51.847 --> 18:54.058
I see. It's fine then.

18:54.725 --> 18:58.395
I'm strong with alcohol anyway,
and this isn't even alcohol.

18:58.395 --> 19:00.731
It's just rubbing alcohol,
so how can I get drunk.

19:00.940 --> 19:03.275
Besides, I stay rational
even when I'm drunk...

19:03.275 --> 19:05.694
So there isn't a single
problem, nothing at all.

19:06.487 --> 19:07.279
Chisa?

19:07.279 --> 19:08.197
What is it?

19:08.197 --> 19:09.907
Look this way for a second.

19:14.411 --> 19:15.120
Huh?

19:19.875 --> 19:21.085
I can't stand.

19:21.168 --> 19:23.671
I told you so.

19:24.505 --> 19:27.925
Sorry, Chisa's drunk,
so I'll carry her up.

19:27.925 --> 19:29.051
Gotcha.

19:36.767 --> 19:38.769
So Iori, that's why...

19:38.769 --> 19:42.815
if you don't use it regularly, the
battery will die when you need it.

19:43.148 --> 19:45.901
The solar powered ones
are more convenient.

19:45.901 --> 19:47.736
Ahh, yeah, yeah.

19:48.112 --> 19:49.238
Are you listening?

19:49.238 --> 19:51.198
I'm listening.

19:51.532 --> 19:55.286
When you're off the bottom,
your fins point downward.

19:55.536 --> 19:58.747
You're so rough about
it and kicks up the sand.

19:59.540 --> 20:02.126
Honestly, I'm
looking out for you,

20:02.126 --> 20:03.502
so be a little grateful.

20:03.502 --> 20:05.087
No way, in your dreams.

20:05.087 --> 20:06.255
Why not?

20:06.255 --> 20:08.507
Because you're indebted to me.

20:10.676 --> 20:11.927
No, I'm not.

20:11.927 --> 20:13.470
You are! Twice over!

20:14.722 --> 20:16.432
What should I do
to pay you back?

20:16.640 --> 20:18.767
You don't even know that?

20:18.767 --> 20:19.977
How should I know?

20:20.227 --> 20:22.855
Honestly, you're such an idiot.

20:22.855 --> 20:24.064
Yeah, yeah.

20:24.064 --> 20:26.442
Listen, from now
on you have to...

20:26.442 --> 20:29.028
start working part-time
and save money.

20:29.028 --> 20:29.737
Huh?

20:30.070 --> 20:32.698
Are you telling me to
pay you back with money?

20:32.698 --> 20:34.617
No! You idiot!

20:34.617 --> 20:35.659
Ouch!

20:39.038 --> 20:41.540
If everyone goes diving...

20:42.958 --> 20:45.169
because you're an idiot...

20:45.169 --> 20:45.794
Hey!

20:46.086 --> 20:49.006
you'll definitely be broke...

20:49.215 --> 20:50.716
and won't be able to go.

20:51.050 --> 20:55.721
And then, you'll feel
lonely like last time.

20:57.765 --> 20:58.641
Chisa?

21:02.520 --> 21:04.396
Like last time?

21:10.528 --> 21:12.071
So that's what it was.

21:14.865 --> 21:16.742
You're so meddlesome.

21:17.076 --> 21:18.077
Geez.

21:22.498 --> 21:23.916
Well, I'm off.

21:23.916 --> 21:25.376
Take care.

21:27.461 --> 21:29.797
Huh? Is Iori busy today?

21:30.130 --> 21:33.050
Yeah, he's starting
a part-time job.

21:33.926 --> 21:35.261
Huh...

21:38.389 --> 21:40.558
This is our new recruit.

21:40.558 --> 21:42.685
I'm starting today, my
name is Iori Kitahara.

21:43.269 --> 21:44.895
I'll do my best and work hard.

21:45.104 --> 21:46.772
I look forward to
working with every-

21:48.941 --> 21:49.817
one?

21:50.067 --> 21:51.610
What do you think you're doing?

21:52.194 --> 21:53.237
Oh my.

21:53.237 --> 21:56.907
Would you rather I
pour beer instead?

22:01.328 --> 22:03.581
Thanks for everything.

22:04.331 --> 22:07.167
Come on, wait a minute.

22:08.085 --> 22:11.255
Let's get along
from here on out.

22:12.089 --> 22:13.257
Kouhai.

22:21.682 --> 22:23.225
Wanna talk to you,
wanna talk to you

22:23.225 --> 22:25.102
First I gotta know all
about you, isn't that right?

22:25.102 --> 22:27.062
Ending it off at round
one reeks of boredom

22:27.062 --> 22:28.814
Rounds two, three,
and four is the plan

22:28.814 --> 22:30.524
As the night gets deeper,
true thoughts escape

22:30.524 --> 22:32.443
Let us go on and on
and dive down late

22:32.443 --> 22:35.446
Your history, your scenery, for
me will your pages get slippery

22:35.446 --> 22:37.489
Hey, show me even more

22:37.489 --> 22:39.241
This is my track and
you are the featured guest

22:39.241 --> 22:40.826
We'll forget by the
time when the dawn hits

22:40.826 --> 22:42.286
Being incomplete is perfection

22:42.286 --> 22:44.538
Hey, show me even more

22:44.538 --> 22:46.123
My mouth keeps slipping,
my mouth keeps slipping

22:46.123 --> 22:47.750
Complaint whether
we sober upward

22:47.750 --> 22:49.793
For now, let's ride
high on this feeling

22:50.169 --> 22:56.217
Let's live this moment with all we
can without leaving a single regret,

22:56.717 --> 22:58.427
We are gonna do it,
we go past the limit now

22:58.427 --> 23:00.054
Not just the whole night,
party till the sun is out

23:00.054 --> 23:02.223
Let's fly high

23:02.223 --> 23:02.806
(Let's fly high)

23:02.806 --> 23:04.808
So first, you just strip it down

23:04.808 --> 23:07.102
An exposed and
feral kind of bond

23:07.102 --> 23:10.731
It's the way of life's cycle,
let us go way beyond

23:10.731 --> 23:12.358
The very moment that
we met I drop my shy act

23:12.358 --> 23:14.109
I wanna bare it all and
say what I need to say

23:14.109 --> 23:16.111
Do it now...

23:16.904 --> 23:21.200
This is the magic spell that breaks
down each and every single wall

23:21.200 --> 23:24.662
And once you get used to
it, you won't feel a thing at all

23:24.662 --> 23:26.163
Being without clothes
is a mystery I live in

23:26.163 --> 23:27.915
The drinking and chatting
is flowing more freely

23:27.915 --> 23:30.292
Try it now...

23:30.709 --> 23:34.213
And right before you
realize what's going on

23:34.213 --> 23:38.425
Your heart will catch
right up and finally be free

23:44.932 --> 23:49.937
NEXT TIME: COWORKERS
